# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit. This repo is public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/gh/hosts.yml
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.gpg
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*token*
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
**/.env
**/.netrc

# gnupg: the stow package tracks *.conf only. Everything below is key material
# or per-machine state and must never land in a public repo. Belt and braces —
# nothing here is copied in deliberately, this is to catch a stray `cp -r`.
**/.gnupg/private-keys-v1.d/
**/.gnupg/openpgp-revocs.d/
**/.gnupg/crls.d/
**/.gnupg/public-keys.d/
**/.gnupg/*.kbx
**/.gnupg/*.kbx~
**/.gnupg/random_seed
**/.gnupg/*.lock
**/.gnupg/S.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately kept local — see README "What is not tracked"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/micro/syntax/
**/noctalia/plugins/
**/polychromatic/devices/
**/polychromatic/states/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Churn that stow folding can drag in (apps writing into folded directories)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.old
*.swp
*.tmp
*~
*.log
**/buffers/
**/cache/
**/Cache/
**/*history*
**/*.pid
**/*.sock
.DS_Store

# GTK file-manager bookmarks — leak local/work paths
**/gtk-3.0/bookmarks

# fish rewrites its universal-variable file live; it cannot be a symlink.
# Seeded from meta/fish_variables.seed instead.
**/fish/fish_variables

# Daemon-managed hardware config, kept local
**/noisetorch/
**/openrazer/

# Polychromatic — device-bound, kept local
**/polychromatic/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wallpaper-driven theme output (Noctalia template engine).
# GTK is the only app driven by the wallpaper here — terminals (kitty/alacritty/
# btop) were deliberately kept on their static curated themes, because a palette
# derived from a wallpaper is not tuned for terminal legibility. These GTK files
# regenerate on every wallpaper change and are written THROUGH stow-folded
# symlinks into the repo (~/.config/gtk-3.0 -> theme/adw-dark/.config/gtk-3.0).
# Derived state, not dotfiles — see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-18-wallpaper-driven-theming-design.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/gtk-3.0/noctalia.css
**/gtk-3.0/gtk.css
**/gtk-4.0/noctalia.css
**/gtk-4.0/gtk.css
# nodeterm canvas layout and agent session ids for this checkout
.nodeterm/
